display_name="HDMI Display"
desc="Independent multi-screen output for Fygo OS: each HDMI/DP connector gets its own DRM/KMS pipeline, fed by a video stream, image, VNC/VM console, local desktop, web page, dashboard or picture-in-picture. Managed from a built-in web panel. Linux DRM/KMS direct scanout, no desktop required. Web-page sources need xvfb and chromium; VNC input routing uses /dev/input."
changelog="1.0.29: Replaced the WenQuanYi Zen Hei bitmap font with Noto Sans CJK SC (SIL OFL 1.1), regenerated the complete GB2312 16x16 table for clearer glyphs, and kept the same table-lookup rendering path (no runtime performance cost). The fpk now ships the OFL and third-party notices. Measured with three outputs (test pattern + image): 30/30/4 fps, 29-32% CPU, stable 193 MB RSS, no error logs. 1.0.28: Fixed inverted Caps Lock on web sources: Xvfb can start with Caps Lock on while the physical keyboard is off, so the X server Caps state is now synchronised before each key. VNC keyboard input also tracks Shift and Caps Lock and sends the correct case and shifted symbols. Remote connection remains one source with automatic RDP/VNC detection and local VM discovery. 1.0.27: RDP and VNC are merged into one Remote connection source, and the backend detects the protocol from the address: user:password@host is RDP; host:port or a local socket path is VNC. The RDP:/VNC: prefixes are no longer required. Local VM consoles in /var/run/vms/*.vnc.sock are detected automatically and appear in a VM picker, so multiple VMs can be chosen without typing the socket path. VNC keyboard input now tracks Shift and Caps Lock and sends the correct case and shifted symbols, fixing guests that only received lowercase letters. The input-device panel now sits above the usage notes, with the notes at the bottom. Switching the source type restores the last successfully used address for that screen and type; a type that was never used shows only its input hint and is no longer overwritten by stale state. 1.0.25: Code review and stability pass. Static/idle sources now refresh once a second (HUD still hides on time and the watchdog no longer reopens paused video or idle VNC/web), the config is written atomically, Chromium profiles are deleted on web stop, DRM master is re-acquired if a compositor releases it, input threads are created safely, audio write errors cannot spin the audio thread, panel state is cleared on stop, and the mobile/panel state buffer is larger. Dead code removed; clean -Wall -Wextra build with zero warnings. Upgrade/config settings (port, compositor policy) are saved so an App Center upgrade preserves them, and configuring the app no longer silently disables the compositor stop option. 1.0.24: fnOS lifecycle compliance. A fresh install opens/runs the app (fnOS shows Open); App Center stop stops and disables it (shows Enable); start enables and starts it; update/config changes preserve the previous state (a running app restarts, a stopped app stays stopped). Uninstall always removes the unit and drop-ins, socket, runtime directory and Chromium profile temp files, and by default also removes the configuration, app data and app directory; the uninstall wizard defaults to a clean uninstall. 1.0.23: The install/config wizard can install xvfb and chromium from the Debian apt repository in one step (the fnOS App Center does not provide them); choose it at install or later. RDP stays on the stable LAN/AVC444/FastPath baseline with the full desktop look (themes, animations, wallpaper, font smoothing); AVC444v2 and extra cache profiles were tested on the Windows server and rejected the session, so they are not enabled. 1.0.22: Slim release. The portable fpk now bundles a minimal FFmpeg built only from the components the app uses (H.264/HEVC/MPEG-2/MPEG-4/VC-1/WMV3/VP8/VP9/AV1/MJPEG/PNG/BMP/GIF + AAC/MP3/AC3/EAC3/DTS/TrueHD/FLAC/Opus/Vorbis/PCM, mov/matroska/mpegts/avi/flv/rtsp/hls/image2 demuxers, file/http/https/rtsp/rtmp protocols, x11grab/fbdev, VAAPI, and the MJPEG preview encoder) instead of the distro FFmpeg with all encoders/filters/third-party codec libraries. Package size drops by roughly 85 MB. Obsolete CMake/virtual-backend/wallctl/build.sh files and old packaging scripts were removed; README/packaging docs updated. 1.0.21: The input-device panel now lists only sources that consume keyboard/mouse: full-screen RDP, VNC and web, plus picture-in-picture when its main or overlay layer is one of those. PiP pointer input is mapped into the small window (clicks outside it do not reach the VNC behind), and the keyboard follows the layer the pointer last entered. The Apply and Stop buttons are now a filled blue primary button and a red-tinted stop button. 1.0.20: The on-screen HUD and waiting screen now render UTF-8 Chinese with an embedded 16x16 GB2312 bitmap font (WenQuanYi Zen Hei), so Chinese file paths are displayed correctly instead of ? or tofu, with no font dependency on the host. The HUD still hides four seconds after a normal source starts. 1.0.19: The video HUD (the LIVE VIEW/REC top bar and the source/codec bottom bar) now hides four seconds after a video, stream, image or picture-in-picture source starts, and returns when the source is re-applied. Non-ASCII paths in the HUD are collapsed to ? instead of being drawn as bitmap garbage. 1.0.18: Keyboard and mouse bound to a web-page source are now injected into Chromium through XTEST (pointer, buttons, wheel, keys and key repeat), so the wall web page can be clicked and typed on directly. The web source now handles X display 0, uses an isolated Chromium profile, and no longer draws the LIVE VIEW HUD over web/VNC mirrors. 1.0.17: The admin panel is now a static web app in app/web, served with content-hash cache busting. It is available through the app own fnOS gateway socket (/app/hdmi-display, an admin-only iframe window) and directly on the configured HTTP port as a fallback; a busy port no longer disables the gateway. Relative API paths make both outputs identical. RDP audio now enables every IEC958 HDMI switch (the connected converter may be index 2) and uses a 50 ms ALSA buffer for tighter lip sync. 1.0.16: RDP audio is redirected to the output HDMI PCM through a private rdpsnd backend. The ALSA device is passed as a comma-free dev:cXdY token so FreeRDP /sound parsing cannot fail, and audio uses a 100 ms buffer for A/V sync. The mouse wheel now sends 120-unit RDP notches (normal scroll speed), the cursor is composited on every presented frame, and high-rate mouse motion is coalesced. 1.0.15: RDP now uses libfreerdp directly instead of an Xvfb + xfreerdp + XTest pipeline. Video is decoded straight into the DRM framebuffer, and keyboard/mouse input is sent as native RDP scancodes and pointer events: letters and the numeric keypad no longer depend on an X keymap, the host keyboard layout is announced from /etc/default/keyboard, and the server cursor shape is composited locally. The cursor is overlaid on every presented frame, so pointer movement no longer waits for a guest repaint; mouse buttons and the wheel are sent as native RDP pointer events with fast-path input; 1000 Hz gaming-mouse motion is coalesced. RDP defaults to the console (+admin) session; append ?normal to the address for an independent session. Every output still starts on the test pattern. 1.0.14: Every connected output now always starts on the test pattern; saved output sources are not auto-applied at boot, and the user chooses each screen source in the panel afterwards. 1.0.13: Keyboard detection now scans every /dev/input/event* node, so devices without a by-id symlink are found; duplicate interfaces are deduped by physical path + role and the specific -event-kbd/-event-mouse node is preferred, fixing unbound keys. Keyboard layout is read from /etc/default/keyboard (XKBLAYOUT) instead of being hardcoded, and the matching RDP layout id is used; enable-rdp.ps1 now adds an English (US) keyboard and makes it the default input method so a zh-CN Pinyin IME does not scramble RDP typing. Unconfigured outputs always start on the test pattern. 1.0.12: Fixed RDP keyboard mapping: Xvfb now starts with a US pc105 keymap, xfreerdp uses RDP layout 0x409 (US), and stuck Shift/Ctrl/Alt modifiers are cleared on connect. 1.0.11: Input devices are classified by evdev capabilities and name: keyboard, mouse, touchpad, touchscreen, tablet, gamepad, media keys, mouse macro keys, system keys, remote. Physical receivers are shown once with all their real roles and purposes; the default view picks one keyboard and one mouse. 1.0.10: Input panel shows exactly one keyboard and one mouse (auto-selected by recent activity, with a Show All toggle) and singular type badges; unused receivers stay hidden. 1.0.9: Input devices are grouped by physical receiver (keyboard+mouse interfaces of one dongle become one row) and type badges are vertically centered; the waiting screen spinner and text are centered as a block. 1.0.8: Input devices are classified as keyboard, mouse or combo in the panel (colored type badge), using evdev EV_KEY/EV_REL capabilities; RDP cursor now uses the real X cursor via XFixes with a standard arrow fallback instead of the old circle. 1.0.7: RDP-only release. Removed the custom Windows agent and its downloads; the remote desktop is Microsoft RDP via bundled FreeRDP. RDP capture now uses XShm (zero-copy X framebuffer), xfreerdp/Xvfb run at raised priority, previews encode at 1 fps, and the pipeline captures at display refresh without a 30 fps cap. Native resolution, 60 fps with DWMFRAMEINTERVAL=15. 1.0.6: Microsoft RDP source (FreeRDP + Xvfb) with native 1920x1080 resolution, 60 fps (after DWMFRAMEINTERVAL=15 on the Windows host), XGetImage capture and XTest input. New panel type '远程桌面（RDP）' and a Windows enable-rdp.ps1 helper (enables RDP, firewall, 60 fps cap). The Windows agent now handles input on a dedicated thread (measured 0.4 ms median pointer latency) and targets 60 fps. 1.0.5: built-in low-latency remote desktop. A small self-contained Windows agent (agent.exe, H.264 + TCP + SendInput, download and install from the web panel) streams a Windows host to any output; keyboard, mouse and wheel are routed back. The agent captures at up to 1080p with static-frame suppression and adaptive cursor overlay. Panel source type 'remote' added; legacy VNC sessions stay available as '虚拟机（旧）'. 1.0.4: multi-GPU output. The app opens every /dev/dri/card*, enumerates all connectors and names them cardN-CONNECTOR, so the iGPU and a discrete GPU can drive screens at the same time (tested with three 1080p displays: 25/30fps). Per-output HDMI audio is matched to the right GPU by EDID/ELD monitor name and PCI slot. 1.0.3: VAAPI hardware decoding enabled by default with software fallback. 1.0.2: native-resolution output, in-process audio with A/V sync, PTS pacing for live streams, cached canvas + non-temporal copy. 1.0.1: hotplug improvements, only connected displays listed. 1.0.0: first release."

